{"kind":"stack","id":"s-repro","title":"Reproduction in plants and animals","theme":{"background":"#f4fbf2","foreground":"#1d3b1f","font":"Comic Sans MS, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Reproduction"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"Living things make new living things of their own kind. This keeps a species going."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Pollination"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"Pollen moves from the male part of a flower to the female part. Bees, wind and water can carry it."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which part of a flower makes the pollen?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"The stamen","why":"The stamen is the male part and makes the pollen.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"The stigma","why":"Pupils mix up the stigma with the stamen; the stigma receives pollen.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"The petal","why":"Petals attract insects but do not make pollen.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"seed"},{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"What is a seed?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"A baby plant inside a protective coat","why":"A seed holds a young plant and a food store inside a coat.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"A flower that has fallen off","why":"Pupils confuse fallen flowers with seeds; flowers are not seeds.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"A root that grows underground","why":"Pupils mix up roots, which take in water, with seeds.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"How does a frog start its life?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"From eggs laid in water","why":"Frogs lay eggs in water, which hatch into tadpoles.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"From seeds dropped by the parent","why":"Seeds belong to plants, not frogs.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-c","label":"Born fully grown from the parent","why":"Pupils think all animals look like their parents from birth; frogs change as they grow.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"You find a bee visiting a flower in the garden. Which path will you follow?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"Follow the bee to see the pollen move","why":"Choice","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Look for seeds on the plant instead","why":"Choice","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"The bee carries pollen to another flower. Now that flower can make seeds. Well done for watching closely!"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"You find a ripe seed head. Seeds drop and may grow into new plants. Nice choice!"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Which animal grows from a fertilised egg laid by its parent?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"A chicken","why":"Chickens hatch from fertilised eggs laid by hens.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"A dog","why":"Dogs are born live from their mother, not from eggs.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"A horse","why":"Horses are born live, which pupils may not realise.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"What is the male cell in reproduction that joins with the female cell?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Sperm","why":"Sperm is the male cell that fertilises the female egg.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Pollen","why":"Pollen is the plant male cell, not an animal one.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Seed","why":"A seed is a plant structure, not a male cell.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done! You finished the reproduction lesson."},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Great work. Living things keep their kind going by making new life."}],"actions":[]}}
